  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IMPLEMENTATION FOR THE NATIONAL STRATEGY FOR THE CONS OF SHOREBIRDS PHASE III</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will: 1) strengthen institutional capacities in the Northern and Central Plateau and the State of Chiapas by training experts who will be responsible for implementing the monitoring protocol that will generate the basic information necessary to support decision-making concerning management and conservation of shorebirds; 2) establish a monitoring network that generates systematized information over time on the abundance and composition of species, by using a standard monitoring protocol and information on the habitat quality at priority and potential sites; and, 3) generate the information that will support decisions concerning conservation and management of shorebirds and their habitats which will support future exercises in prioritization that lead to specific actions for the conservation of the wetlands utilized by shorebirds in the long term.</narrative>
  </description>
